Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Inhibition", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"037e842b-c8ee-48e2-bb4d-df44c1e8e7ba"],

Cell["\<\
Positive set elements (i > 0) denote excitatory neurons, whereas their \
negative counterparts (-i) are inhibitory.  All circuit components  properly \
handle the presence of negative elements. Only multiset paths (tagged  \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]multiset\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]) convey inhibitory \
signals.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"86bacf56-0403-42ec-ab6a-104e037a1bbe"],

Cell["\<\
In this framework, the only source of negative set elements (apart from \
external inputs) are paths tagged as \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]inhibit\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. This  circuit flips positives into negatives, \
preserving the negatives:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ce751fec-62fd-41a5-8d40-9b660b28d698"],

